title The machinery that read the elder room, and the meters that rose on their own proofs
prompt Read KYRI and RADIANT_STYLE first, then REMEMBER and the itineraries and the top three log rows; Standfast on reds; take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first; deep-read one council-rota row; refresh REMEMBER; send often.
think The running thread handed the crux directly. The last lap closed REDS %153 on twenty-six document links resolving through an untracked `work-in-progress -> crux` symlink, and its recommend line asked the sharper question rather than answering it -- which OTHER guards read the filesystem where they mean to read the repository, since living_docs_lint's own broken-link duty still tests with `[ -e ]` and is one of several.
think Council rota row 3 -- Water/Venus, care and flow: Gall's Law, the happy zone and the thin edge, growing a language. Gall settled the shape of the answer before the answer existed. tools/fixtures/tracked_link_scan.sh already worked and already built the set of paths a fresh clone carries; a complex meter designed from scratch would charge the build twice. So the new guard is the same simple working thing grown one duty wider, in its own file, reading its own concern.
think The happy zone named the boundary. A path literal inside a tool source is a pure fold -- text in, verdict out, no world required -- so it belongs in the fast isolated center, and the only thin-edge fact needed is `git ls-files`. That is why the control could build real git repositories rather than mimic one: the edge is small enough to stand up eight times in a temporary pen.
think Measured before restrategizing. A census extracted path-like tokens from all 2,669 tracked tools/**.rish and tools/**.sh, built the known-path set from `git ls-files` plus every ancestor directory plus the declared submodules, and asked which literals resolve on this pier while standing outside it. The answer was 116 literals across 58 files, every one reading the elder room through the untracked symlink.
think The four worst were load-bearing. tools/fixtures/reds_first_scan.sh set ledger="work-in-progress/REDS.md" -- the reds-first guard reading the ledger through the symlink. tools/compass_rose.rish printed NOW_OK from a bare `test -f work-in-progress/TASKS.md`, which is the `[ -e ]` class again, in the compass itself. tools/fixtures/radiant_lint_scan.sh named three living cards there. And `.brix`, the descriptor listing the bricks Mantra tracks, carried `file work-in-progress/ROADMAP.md` and `file work-in-progress/TASKS.md`.
think Scoped the repoint to non-comment lines on purpose. Several of these guards explain the breach that shaped them in their header prose, and tracked_link_scan.sh's whole WHY block names the elder room a dozen times. A sweep that rewrote comments would delete the record of why the guards exist, so the rule became: repoint what a tool READS, leave what a tool SAYS.
think Running the two touched guards found both already red at HEAD, proven by stashing the round and re-running -- width_check_th4 pinned to a .brix version that molted thirteen days ago, compass_rose demanding a literal word a Radiant pass had reworded. Neither is on the roster, which is why neither was noticed. That is the third firing of one lantern after %147 and %150.
think Both repaired per sense rather than by loosening. The version pin follows the living value with the molt named beside it; the word match became `supersed|replaced`, binding to the supersession FACT the document states rather than to one spelling. Same choice REDS %151 made a lap earlier.
think Then two meters rose on their own proofs, which is the lap's second theme. The dated_path census stood red at HEAD at 193 against a ceiling of 192, because the previous lap's SESSION LOG quoted its control's planted filename `20260101-000000_a-dated-note.md` while the exclusion list exempts only the control file. And the new phantom_path guard reddened on its own seating run, from its own control planting `work-in-progress/REMEMBER.md`. Same lesson, two lists, one lap.
obs The mechanism: tools/fixtures/phantom_path_scan.sh builds the known-path set from `git ls-files`, every ancestor directory derived by awk, and the submodule paths read out of .gitmodules; selects tracked `tools/**.rish`, `tools/**.sh`, and `.brix` as sources, dropping `*_control.sh`; extracts path-like tokens with an awk match loop from lines whose first non-space character is not `#`; and gates at zero every token that fails membership yet satisfies `[ -e ]`. tools/phantom_path_witness.rish drives the scan and tools/fixtures/phantom_path_control.sh, asserting each verdict by name.
obs Following a tracked symlink is a composition rather than a new promise. `pond/apps/brushstroke` is a tracked symlink into the tracked `brushstroke/` room, so `pond/apps/brushstroke/wayland_seed.rye` resolves perfectly for a reader who clones -- it was the scan's one false positive on first run. The fix reads .gitmodules-style prefix substitution off `git ls-files -s` mode 120000 entries, which is sound precisely because tracked_link_witness already gates every tracked symlink at landing inside the tree.
obs Four readings pass free by named rule, each with its reason stated in the scan's own head: `vendor/` is provisioned by submodule or fetch_toolchain; `seed/` is the depersonalized projection, gitignored by design; a dot-segment names a generated or machine-local room; and a literal resolving NOWHERE belongs to dated_path_witness -- one duty, one guard, so two can never come to disagree.
obs The comment exemption is proven rather than asserted. The control's third case plants `work-in-progress/REMEMBER.md` inside a comment in a throwaway repository and requires the scan to pass free, because a guard must always be able to name the breach that created it -- including this one, whose own prose names the elder room a dozen times.
obs REDS %157's repair moved the exemption from the address to the name. DP_FIXTURE_BASENAMES subtracts a planted basename wherever it is quoted, which is safe exactly because such a name is built to match nothing: a stamp of all zeros names no lap this tree ever ran. The census returned to its exact 192 baseline and the ceiling never moved, which is the discipline -- a ceiling that rises to meet a number has stopped being a ceiling.
obs Booking five rows carried crux/REDS.md well past its 24,576-byte bound, so rows %152 and %153-%154 folded to crux/archive/ with doorway lines written in the same act and every relative link repointed one level deeper. The monotone guard then refused twice on the way, once for the span and once for the fold list, which is the fourth lap running that a ledger guard has corrected a hand.
obs What this does not prove: that a tool reads the RIGHT file, only that the file is one a fresh clone carries. And the wider gap is named rather than carried -- twenty-three rostered guards stand against 1,654 witnesses, so the roster is a sample, and three of the reds closed this lap surfaced only because a repoint happened to touch the file.
file tools/fixtures/phantom_path_scan.sh the reading -- every path literal a tracked tool or .brix reads, gated against the set a fresh clone carries
file tools/fixtures/phantom_path_control.sh eight behaviors on real throwaway git repositories, two refusals bitten and six honest readings left free
file tools/phantom_path_witness.rish the rung -- drives both, asserts each verdict by name, and states what it does not prove
file .brix the descriptor's two bricks repointed from the elder room to crux/
file tools/fixtures/reds_first_scan.sh the reds-first guard now reads crux/REDS.md rather than the symlink
file tools/compass_rose.rish the compass reads crux/, and its settlement clause binds to the supersession fact rather than one spelling
file tools/width_check_th4.rish the .brix version pin follows the living 20260810.145743, with the molt named beside it
file tools/fixtures/dated_path_exclusions.sh DP_FIXTURE_BASENAMES -- an exemption that follows the planted name rather than its address
file tools/fixtures/dated_path_scan.sh subtracts each planted fixture basename wherever it is quoted
file crux/REDS.md rows %155-%158 booked and closed, rows %152 and %153-%154 folded to archive under the bound
file crux/standing-equipment.kyri phantom_path seated as the roster's twenty-third guard
file crux/REMEMBER.md Now refilled with the live work-front and the open roster-coverage question
loom witness=phantom_path sources=2649 literals=7604 phantom=0
loom roster=standing_equipment guards=23 green=23 red=0
loom census=dated_path refs_home=11629 refs_lost=192 ceiling=192
recommend keep-going the ladder arc's queue is unchanged and waiting -- rests_path leads the free-absolutely reading at 250 over eleven rungs, confer_words holds the queue's free head at 294 over forty-three rungs priced at forty-three import re-exports, and answered_by still leads by return at 330 costing sixty-eight openings. Beside it this lap answers the question the last one opened -- the machinery read the elder room in 116 places and now cannot -- and leaves a sharper one standing in plain sight: twenty-three rostered guards against 1,654 witnesses means the roster is a sample nobody has chosen, and three of this lap's four reds were found only because a repoint happened to touch the file. The honest next meter asks which witnesses earn the roster, so a guard's coverage stops depending on where the last sweep wandered.
